1
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:14,190
Fifteen students test their reaction times, in hundredths of a second.

2
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:22,840
The results are 24, 31, 19, 27, 35, 22, 28, 41, 26, 33, 29, 18, 37, 25 and 30.

3
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:28,510
How could you show every value in order, and still see the shape of the data?

4
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:31,610
Which diagram keeps all the values in order?

5
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:34,910
Pause the video and choose.

6
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:36,530
A stem-and-leaf diagram.

7
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:41,140
The tens digit is the stem, and the units digit is the leaf.

8
00:00:41,190 --> 00:00:46,550
Remember: the median is the middle value, when the values are in order.

9
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:49,900
The range is the largest minus the smallest.

10
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:51,820
41 minus 18 is 23.

11
00:00:51,870 --> 00:00:53,790
Write the stems in a column.

12
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:57,520
Write each leaf next to its stem, in order, lined up.

13
00:00:57,570 --> 00:01:01,240
Always give a key, like: 2, leaf 4, means 24.

14
00:01:01,290 --> 00:01:06,630
It keeps every value, and it shows the shape like a bar chart on its side.

15
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:07,360
Your turn.

16
00:01:07,410 --> 00:01:08,800
There are 15 values.

17
00:01:08,850 --> 00:01:10,180
What is the median?

18
00:01:10,230 --> 00:01:13,540
Pause the video and try it.

19
00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:17,490
With 15 values, the median is the 8th.

20
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:22,570
Count along: 18, 19, then 22, 24, 25, 26, 27, 28.

21
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:24,890
The median is 28.

22
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:30,940
The mean is the sum, 425, divided by 15, which is about 28.3.

23
00:01:30,990 --> 00:01:32,240
Here is the method.

24
00:01:32,290 --> 00:01:37,520
Step 1: choose the stems, often the tens, and write them in a column.

25
00:01:37,570 --> 00:01:40,330
Step 2: write each leaf next to its stem.

26
00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:43,610
Then redraw it with the leaves in order.

27
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:47,070
Step 3: line up the leaves, and add a key.

28
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:50,770
Step 4: read off the median, mode and range.

29
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:56,510
Draw a diagram for 52, 47, 61, 55, 49, 58, 63 and 50.

30
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:59,770
The stems are 4, 5 and 6.

31
00:01:59,820 --> 00:02:06,150
There are 8 values, so the median is halfway between the 4th and the 5th values.

32
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:06,840
Your turn.

33
00:02:06,890 --> 00:02:09,400
What is the median of these 8 values?

34
00:02:09,450 --> 00:02:12,320
Pause and work it out.

35
00:02:12,370 --> 00:02:14,630
52 plus 55 is 107.

36
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:17,110
Halve it: 53.5.

37
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:19,170
A key can show decimals.

38
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:27,180
If 3, leaf 4, means 3.4 kilograms, then 3 with leaves 1, 4, 4, 8 means 3.1, 3.4, 3.4 and 3.8.

39
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:31,340
The mode is 3.4, because it appears twice.

40
00:02:31,390 --> 00:02:35,720
Kai draws a stem-and-leaf diagram for 34, 31 and 38.

41
00:02:35,770 --> 00:02:37,950
Which line is wrong?

42
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,050
Line 1 is wrong.

43
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:42,950
The leaves are not in order, and there is no key.

44
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:48,980
It should be 3, leaves 1, 4, 8, with a key: 3, leaf 1, means 31.

45
00:02:49,030 --> 00:02:52,510
Some railway timetables are stem-and-leaf diagrams!

46
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:57,980
The hour is the stem, and the minutes of each departure are the leaves.

47
00:02:58,030 --> 00:02:59,180
One last question.

48
00:02:59,230 --> 00:03:02,260
What does a stem-and-leaf diagram always need?

49
00:03:02,310 --> 00:03:05,460
Pause the video and choose.

50
00:03:05,510 --> 00:03:10,370
It always needs a key, so that readers know what the numbers mean.

51
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:16,000
To remember: the stem is the leading digit, and the leaf is the last digit.

52
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:18,720
Leaves go in order, and lined up.

53
00:03:18,770 --> 00:03:20,890
Always give a key.

54
00:03:20,940 --> 00:03:25,440
Find the median, mode and range straight from the diagram.

55
00:03:25,490 --> 00:03:30,830
Great work! Now practise lesson 16.3 on Camday.
